  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 217 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nMainly a dry forecast for the most part through the extended\nperiod. However, a shortwave over the Four Corners is progged\nto drop southeast across West Texas on Thursday, with a potential\nclosed low developing over the Edwards Plateau region by the end \nof the week. This system may result in some rain chances primarily\nacross southern portions of the forecast area Thursday night into\nFriday. At this time, NBM low POPs (20%) seem reasonable across \nthe I-10 corridor but this system will need to be monitored for \npotentially higher rain chances for the area as the week \nprogresses. Temperatures are expected to be slightly above normal \nthrough the upcoming weekend, with highs in the upper 80s and \nlower 90s. Overnight lows will be in the upper 50s and lower 60s \nthrough Wednesday night, warming into the mid and upper 60s by\nthe weekend.",
